# ESP32 only supports 2.4GHz WiFi, not 5GHz. Make sure your router has the 2.4G band enabled
# WiFi password must be at least 8 characters long. If your router's password is too short, change the router password or use a different network
# Connecting to public WiFi (such as cafes, campus nteworks) may require web authentication (Portal), which the ESP32 cannot complete. Use an open or WPA2-encrypted network
# When the SSID contains Chinese or special characters, encoding issues may occur. It's recommended to use an SSID with only English letters and numbers
WIFI_PASSWORD=<your_wifi_password>
WIFI_SSID=<your_wifi_ssid>